# cbcl -- Concatenated Base Call Files
aggregated BCL data; Tiles from the same lane and surface are aggregated into one CBCL file for each lane and surface.
CBCL Header
 u16 Bytes 0–1 Version number, current version is 1 unsigned 16 bits little endian integer
 u32 Bytes 2–5 Header size unsigned 32 bits little endian integer
 u8 Byte 6 Number of bits per base call unsigned
 u8 Byte 7 Number of bits per q-score unsigned
q-val mapping info
 u32 Bytes 0–3 Number of bins (B), zero indicates no mapping B pairs of 4 byte values (if B > 0) {from, to}, {from, to}, {from, to} …
	 from: quality score bin
	 to: quality score
 u32 Number of tile records unsigned 32 bits little endian integer gzip virtual file offsets, one record per tile
 u32 Bytes 0–3: tile number
 u32 Bytes 4–7 Number of clusters written into the current block (required due to bitpacked q-scores)
 u32 Bytes 8–11 Uncompressed block size of the tile data (useful for sanity check when excluding non-PF clusters)
 u32 Bytes 12–15 Compressed block size of the tiledata
 b1 ? non-PF clusters excluded flag 1: non-PF clusters are excluded 0: non-PF clusters are included
GZIP blocks
