# Locs file -- Location Files
(LOCS) are binary files that contain the cluster positions on the flow cell. CLOCS files are compressed versions of LOCS files.
Files appended with  _pos.txt are text-based files containing two columns and a number of rows equal to the
number of clusters. The first column records the X-coordinate and the second column records the Y-coordinate.
Each row ends with <cr><lf>.

# ExtractionMetricsOut.bin -- Per tile per cycle per channel 90th percentile of intensity and FWHM values
Extraction metrics such as FWHM scores and raw intensities
 byte 0: file version number (3)
 byte 1: L, the length of each record
 byte 2: ChannelCount, the channel count
 bytes(N*L+3)-((N+1)*L+2):record:
  2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
  4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
  2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
  4 x ChannelCount bytes: fwhm scores (float) for channels in the order listed in the RunInfo (or [A, C, G, T] for legacy platforms).
	2 x ChannelCount bytes: intensities (uint16) for channel in the order listed in the RunInfo (or [A, C, G, T] for legacy platforms).
Where N is the record index.

# Quality Metrics (QMetricsOut.bin)
The quality metrics file contains the quality score distribution.
 byte 1: length of each record
 byte 2: quality score binning (byte flag representing if binning was on) if (byte 2 == 1) // quality score binning on
 byte 3: number of quality score bins, numBins
forallbinsBfrom1tonumBins:
 byte 4 + 3*(B-1): lower boundary of bin B
 byte 5 + 3*(B-1): upper boundary of bin B u byte 6 + 3*(B-1): remapped scores of bin B
The remaining bytes are for the records, with each record in this format: u 2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
 4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
 2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
 if (byte 2 == 1)
	4x numBinsbytes: numberofclustersassignedtoQ-scorebins1–numBins(uint32)
 else
  4x50 bytes: numberofclustersassignedscoreQ1throughQ50(uint32)

# Error Metrics (ErrorMetricsOut.bin)
The error metrics file contains cycle error rate. Version 3 format contains counts for perfect reads and read with 1–4 errors.
 byte 0: file version number (4)
 byte 1: length of each record (12)
 bytes(N*12+2)-(N*12+13):record:
  2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
  4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
  2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
  4 bytes: error rate (float) Where N is the record index.

# Error Metrics (ErrorMetricsOut.bin) -- version 6
  byte 0: version number (6)
  byte 1: record size (12+4*num_adapter)
Extended Header
    byte 2-3: num_adapter (uint16)
    byte 4-5: adapter_base_cnt (uint16)
    byte 6-(6+num_adapter*adapter_base_cnt) (uint8)
n-Records
    2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
    4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
    2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
    4 bytes: error rate (float32)
    4*num_adapter bytes: vector of fraction of reads adapter-trimmed at the cycle (float32)

# Tile Metrics (TileMetricsOut.bin)
The tile metrics file contains aggregate or read metrics by tile.
 byte 0: file version number (3)
 byte 1: length of each record (15)
 bytes 2–5: area of a tile in mm^2 (float)
 bytes(N*15+6)-(N*15+20):record:
 2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
 4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
 1 byte: metricCode, the metric code (char) u  if(metricCode == 't')
 4 bytes: cluster count (float)
 4 bytes: PF cluster count (float) u else if(metricCode == 'r')
 4 bytes: read number (uint32)
 4 bytes: % aligned (float) u  else if(metricCode == '\0')
 8 bytes:0
Where N is the record index.

# Extended Tile Metrics (ExtendedTileMetricsOut.bin)
The extended tile metrics file contains aggregate or read metrics by tile.
NovaSeq 6000 produces the ExtendedTileMetricsOut.bin file in both the version 2 and 3 formats.
Format for version 3:
 byte 0: file version number (3)
 byte 1: length of each record (18)
 bytes(N*18+2)-(N*18+19):record:
  2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
  4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
  4 bytes: occupied cluster count (float)
  4 bytes: upper left fiducial location in X (float)
	4 bytes: upper left fiducial location in Y(float)
Where N is the record index.
Format for version 2:
 byte 0: file version number (2)
 byte 1: length of each record (10)
 bytes(N*10+2)-(N*10+11):record:
  2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
  4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
  4 bytes: occupied cluster count (float)
Where N is the record index.

# Corrected Intensity Metrics (CorrectedIntMetricsOut.bin)
The corrected intensity metrics file contains base call metrics.
NovaSeq 6000 produces the CorrectedIntMetricsOut.bin file in version 4 format:
 byte 0: file version number (4)
 byte 1: length of each record (28)
 bytes(N*28+2)-(N*28+29):record:
 2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
 4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
 2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
 4 bytes:numberofNoCallbasecalls(uint32)
 4 bytes:numberofAbasecalls(uint32)
 4 bytes:numberofCbasecalls(uint32)
 4 bytes: number of G base calls (uint32)
 4 bytes:numberofTbasecalls(uint32)
Where N is the record index.

# Image Metrics (ImageMetricsOut.bin)
The image metrics file contains minimum and maximum contrast values for images.
NovaSeq 6000
NovaSeq 6000 produces the ImageMetricsOut.bin file in version 3 format:
 byte 0: file version number (3)
 byte 1: length of each record (recordLength, depends on number of channels)
 byte 2: number of channels
 bytes (N * recordLength + 3) - ((N+1) * recordLength + 2): record:
 2 bytes: lane number (uint16)
 4 bytes: tile number (uint32)
 2 bytes: cycle number (uint16)
For each channel in the channel set
 2 bytes: min contrast value for image (uint16) For each channel in the channel set
 2 bytes: max contrast value for image (uint16)
Where N is the record index.

