# SDM Files
NERSC will have the files for the longest period.
files may be incomplete for up to a few days (or longer) after sequencing has released the run (can be weeks-months if concerns about mixups or other issues).
During this time, IGB (and Dori) will have the complete set of files.
The illumina run folder folder is a windows file system, the processing output folder is a linux file system.
there are two illumina file systems, both are mounted at IGB:
Dori all sequencer output: /clusterfs/jgi/illumina/
Dori pipeline output:      /clusterfs/jgi/illumina_processing production/novaseqx
NERSC:  only parts of the FS are synced over to NERSC from IGB. For all practical purposes you can mostly assume these paths to be equivalent:
Dori: /clusterfs/jgi/illumina/staging/*
NERSC: /global/cfs/cdirs/seqfs/prod/illumina/staging/*

# SDM processing
At NERSC folder will be incomplete for the early part of run folders' lifecycle. IGB/Dori will have a shortened lifecycle. So this is what happens:
- When sequencing starts, Illumina starts rsycing the files over to NERSC.
  + This process is halted once processing starts.  The run at NERSC at this point may or may not be complete.
- When the run has completed processing and prod seq has released the files, the rsync process is started up again.
  + The run folder is rsync'ed to completion, this may take days to complete, so any recently sequenced folder is always incomplete.
  + After the run folder is sync'ed over, the processing output folder (which is in a different location on Dori and IGB) is synced into the run folder at NERSC.
- Once syncing is complete, the processing folder at IGB is cleared out.
  + Afterwards the run folder (at IGB/Dori) has parts of it removed in order to make space on the file system for future sequencing.
- After 1-3 months, the run folders at NERSC have the BCL files and fastqs are removed, and the logs, thumbnails, data, and analysis folders are tarred up.
  + After this is complete, the folder is sent to tape.
- After a few more months, the folder at NERSC is removed.
  + Once the folder is removed, what is left of the folder at IGB (and Dori) is removed.

